    "version": 1,
    "caption_draft": "Figure 2. Core safeguards of colabctl. (a) Replacing per-client SSH-over-WS connections with one pre-warmed OpenSSH ControlMaster Unix socket multiplexes terminals, VS Code, -L tunnels, and no-PTY probes over Colab's single slot without HTTP 429. (b) Inside the VM, a detached cost-guard watchdog tracks GPU utilization (<5%), PTY I/O, and hard runtime limits, broadcasting a 2-minute warning (resettable via extend +2h) before autonomously posting $TBE_RUNTIME_ADDR/unassign to halt Compute Unit billing even when the host sleeps or disconnects.",
    "open_questions": [],
    "notes": "Composite double-column mechanism figure with two equal-height parts: (a) baseline vs. ours SSH multiplexing comparison and (b) 4-state autonomous VM cost-guard FSM. Shares the exact blue-orange house palette and typography of colabctl-fig1."
  },
